            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous return of patency in a completely occluded coronary artery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>705-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We observed a 56-year=old man in whom an occluded right coronary artery was observed to be widely patent on a subsequent angiogram 40 months later. This &quot;regression,&quot; which occurred without a change in his risk factors, shows that manipulation of risk factors can be proven to be a cause of regression only in controlled studies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
